      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing KMS as Provider**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud KMS for key management and decryption. Now, I need to figure out how to structure the `decrypt_payload.py` file to effectively interface with the KMS. I am thinking about how to securely store and retrieve the key ID within the script.\n\n\n**Defining KMS Implementation**\n\nI'm solidifying the KMS implementation, opting for Google Cloud KMS and the `google-cloud-kms` library. My next task is coding the `decrypt_payload.py` file. I'm focusing on crafting a `decrypt_payload` function that handles the project ID, location, key ring, key name, and the encrypted ciphertext. I am thinking of the best approach to securely import the KMS client and call the function.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789868046375,
          "start": 1789868044673
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc72f181001BEF2url6Pqktdu",
