      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Cloud KMS Integration**\n\nI'm currently evaluating integrating AWS KMS for key management and encryption in `encrypt_payload.py`. The initial focus is selecting a suitable cloud provider; AWS KMS appears a promising option. Next, I will dive into the implementation details and identify the necessary modules to import.\n\n\n**Initiating Code Generation**\n\nI've determined AWS KMS is the chosen provider and will now begin generating the `encrypt_payload.py` code. The core steps involve importing `boto3`, establishing a KMS client, and defining the `encrypt_payload` function. This function will accept a key ID and plaintext, and then encrypt using `client.encrypt`, returning the ciphertext. The `write` tool will be employed to assemble the python code.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789868041702,
          "start": 1789868039015
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc72db67001dr4gqG8FfY0LKP",
